    "correctAnswerSourceText": "4",
    "explanation": "It is important for clients with allergic rhinitis to determine the precipitating factors so that they can be avoided. Keeping a diary can help identify these triggers. Nasal decongestant sprays should not be used regularly because they can cause a rebound effect. Antibiotics are not appropriate for allergic rhinitis because an infection is not present. Increasing activity will not control the client's symptoms; in fact, walking outdoors may increase them if the client is allergic to pollen. CN: Health promotion and maintenance; CL: Synthesize 8. 7.5 mL CN: Pharmacological and parenteral therapies; CL: Apply",
