    "explanation": "Stressful and emotional events have been clearly linked to exacerbations of ulcerative colitis, although their role in the etiology of the disease has been disproved. A modified vegetarian diet or an exercise program is an unlikely cause of the exacerbation. CN: Physiological adaptation; CL: Apply 22. 31 gtt/min To administer IV fluids at 125 mL/h using tubing that has a drip factor of 15 gtt/mL, the nurse should use the following formula: CN: Pharmacological and parenteral therapies; CL: Apply",
