    "correctAnswerSourceText": "4",
    "explanation": "Signs and symptoms of an external access shunt infection include redness, tenderness, swelling, and drainage from around the shunt site. The absence of a bruit indicates closing of the shunt. Sluggish capillary refill time and coolness of the extremity indicate decreased blood flow to the extremity. CN: Reduction of risk potential; CL: Analyze",
