    "explanation": "The client is suspected of having a sexually transmitted infection. Therefore, the client's sexual history, assessment, and examination must be documented, including symptoms (such as fever, chills, and enlarged glands) and their onset and duration. Allergies are critical to document for every client, but are especially noteworthy in this case because antibiotics will be prescribed. If a sexually transmitted infection is confirmed, sexual contacts need to be treated. To protect privacy, the names and phone numbers should never be placed in the chart. The public health department will also assist in obtaining information and treating known sexual contacts. CN: Safety and infection control; CL: Analyze 69. 4 tablets Next, divide the desired dose by the dose on hand: CN: Pharmacological and parenteral therapies; CL: Apply",
