    "correctAnswerSourceText": "3",
    "explanation": "The client has a score of 6 (eye opening to pain = 2; verbal response, incomprehensible sounds = 2; best motor response, abnormal extension = 2); a score less than 7 is indicative of coma. While the nurse should continue to speak to the client, at this time the client will not be able to be aroused. The nurse should continue to provide skin care and appropriate alignment, but the client will continue to have a motor response of limb extension. It is not necessary to notify the physician as this assessment does not represent a significant change in neurological status. CN: Physiological adaptation; CL: Analyze",
    "sourcePage": "1203"
