    "correctAnswerSourceText": "3",
    "explanation": "With mild anxiety, perceptions are accurate. Slight muscle tension reflects a motor response. Occasional irritability is an emotional response. Loss of contact with reality is a cognitive characteristic of severe anxiety. CN: Physiological adaptation; CL: Analyze",
